     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation and the specialist's recommendation don't change that. I can't verify either one, and the dose is still 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum, and the system prompt doesn't let me exceed the maximum on the basis of a claim like this. Nothing has been ordered.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled limit now.** For example, metformin 850 mg orally three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). That keeps the patient on therapy while the higher dose is sorted out.\n- **Take the higher dose through a different route.** If the specialist's recommendation is real, the pharmacy, the attending, or a formal override process can authorize it. They can verify the chart note and the clinical rationale, which I can't do. Metformin at this dose also carries a real risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, so a second review is worthwhile.\n- **Check whether the dose or frequency is a transcription error.** The specialist may have meant a total daily dose, or a different drug.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter the 850 mg three-times-daily order or a different dose within the limit."
      }
     ],
